Syntax: int sprintf(char *str, const char *string,...); Return: If successful,it returns the total number of characters written excluding null-character appended in the string, in case of failure a negative number is returned .sprintf stands for “String print”. Instead of printing on console, it store output on char buffer which are specified in sprintf. 
            C

    // Example program to demonstrate sprintf()
#include <stdio.h>
int main()
{
    char buffer[50];
    int a = 10, b = 20, c;
    c = a + b;
    sprintf(buffer, "Sum of %d and %d is %d", a, b, c);

    // The string "sum of 10 and 20 is 30" is stored
    // into buffer instead of printing on stdout
    printf("%s", buffer);

    return 0;
}

OutputSum of 10 and 20 is 30Time Complexity: O(n), where n is the number of elements being stored in buffer.Auxiliary Space:  O(n), where n is the number of elements being stored in buffer.
